  "The selected shader": "",
  "These modes cover CyGPUInspector's tools: reading the frame, disabling, highlighting, capturing and replacing shaders. They never give a terminal or access to your files. Changing the mode cancels a pending request. External agents connected through MCP use the permission level of the MCP panel instead.": "",
  "This command bound a descriptor table. Its contents are not readable through the add-on API, so the list below is incomplete.": "",
  "This is the runtime capture: it costs the game a few percent and can be left on. The strip at the top is the last few hundred frames. One frame shows the latest frame on a time axis: the whole frame, its passes, then the commands measured inside them. Continuous shows every measured frame one after another on the GPU clock, with the time the GPU waited between two frames; click a frame in the strip to go to it. Wheel to zoom, drag to pan, double-click to fit or to follow the newest frame again. Lengths need the tracking level to be Pass Timing or higher. Names are derived, never read from the game: no graphics API exposes its debug markers to a ReShade add-on.": "",
